# The home-screen app was serving yesterday's JavaScript. The page and its
# data are rewritten whenever a price moves, so a copy is never used without
# asking: no-cache keeps it but checks it against the server every time, and
# an unchanged file comes back as a 304 with no body (it was no-store, which
# fetched every byte again on every open; Oct 12, 2026).
/*
  Cache-Control: no-cache

# Pictures and icons change by file name or not at all: a month in the phone
# (Jose, Sep 16, 2026: "they load every time")
/faces/*
  ! Cache-Control
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=2592000, immutable
/ico/*
  ! Cache-Control
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=604800
# hls.js, asked for only when a clip plays: a month (Oct 12, 2026)
/lib/*
  ! Cache-Control
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=2592000
